{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <string>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <vector>\n#include <queue>\n#include <limits>\n#include <utility>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <map>\n#include <stack>\n#include <numeric>\n#include <set>\n\n#define endl '\\n'\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nstruct Fraction {\n    ll a, b;\n};\n\npair<ll, ll> geta(int x, int y, int b) {\n    ll lower = (ll)b * x / y;\n    ll upper = ((ll)b * x + (y-1)) / y;\n    return {lower, upper};\n}\n\nll gcd(ll a, ll b) {\n    if (b == 0) return a;\n    return gcd(b, a % b);\n}\n\nvoid solve(int x, int y, int n) {\n    vector<Fraction> cands;\n    for (int b = 1; b <= n; b++) {\n        auto ap = geta(x, y, b);\n        cands.push_back({ap.first, b});\n        cands.push_back({ap.second, b});\n    }\n\n    auto comp = [&](Fraction fa, Fraction fb)-> bool {\n        ll a1 = fa.a;\n        ll b1 = fa.b;\n        ll a2 = fb.a;\n        ll b2 = fb.b;\n\n        ll left = abs(x * b1 * b2 - a1 * b2 * y);\n        ll right = abs(x * b1 * b2 - a2 * b1 * y);\n\n        if (left != right) return left < right;\n\n        if (b1 != b2) return b1 < b2;\n\n        return a1 < a2;\n    };\n\n    sort(cands.begin(), cands.end(), comp);\n\n    cout << cands.front().a << \"/\" << cands.front().b << endl;\n}\n\nint main(){\n    std::ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(0);\n    int x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n\n    solve(x, y, n);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\nfrom fractions import Fraction as PyFraction\n\ndef geta(x, y, b):\n    lower = (b * x) // y\n    upper = ((b * x) + (y - 1)) // y\n    return (lower, upper)\n\ndef solve(x, y, n):\n    cands = []\n    for b in range(1, n + 1):\n        ap = geta(x, y, b)\n        cands.append((ap[0], b))\n        cands.append((ap[1], b))\n    \n    def comp(frac):\n        a1, b1 = frac\n        # Calculate the absolute difference for comparison\n        left = abs(x * b1 - a1 * y)\n        return (left, b1, a1)\n    \n    # Sort using the comparison criteria\n    cands.sort(key=comp)\n    \n    # Output the first element\n    print(f\"{cands[0][0]}/{cands[0][1]}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    x, y, n = map(int, input().split())\n    solve(x, y, n)\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012683063687290996, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -0.02336621843278408, -0.6330860257148743, -0.10051032900810242, -0.03807159513235092, -0.2969346344470978, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.00036173476837575436, -0.11341489851474762, -0.025132229551672935, -0.001116010476835072, -0.01106978952884674, -0.0012575822183862329, -0.010121330618858337, -6.318072337307967e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.9960475482512265e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.6326253414154053, -1.1920922133867862e